	-> git : Git is a distributed version control system (DVCS) used primarily to track changes in source code during software development.
		- git init (add git to folder)
		- rm -rf .git(remove git from folder)
		- git add <file_name>
		- git commit -m "<any_msg>"
		- git status
		- git checkout -b <new_branch_name>
		- git switch <branch_name>
		- git branch
		- git log
		- git restore <file_name>
		- git restore --staged <file_name>
		- git revert <commit_id>
		- git push origin <branch_name>
		- git pull origin <branch_name>
		- git remote add roigin <url_of_the_github_repo>.git
		- git remote -v
		- git remote set-url origin https://[add_token]@github.com/meetgondaliya31/git-github.git
		- git branch -M main
		- git fetch
		- github hooks 
		- git remote -v : view remote origin
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
		
